'' '#import "vendor/alpha" link static' (tiko-vendor RFC-0002 V4-V7): the module's unit has
'' TIKO_LINK_STATIC, so its static '#foreignlib' branch links alpha's archive (alpha_id 1),
'' and the header it carries reads the same macro in the importer (V12). Nothing is copied.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' ENV: TKO_PKG=build/.vls/pkg
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.vls/mc
'' CLEAN: build/.vls
'' COPY: tests/modules/src/vlink/pkg => build/.vls/pkg
'' STEP: -target windows-x86_64 -lib tests/modules/src/vlink/libsrc/alpha_static.tiko -o build/.vls/pkg/vendor/alpha/lib/alpha_windows_x86_64.a
'' STEP: -target windows-x86_64 -dll tests/modules/src/vlink/libsrc/alpha_dynamic.tiko -o build/.vls/pkg/vendor/alpha/lib/alpha_windows_x86_64.dll
'' STEP: -target windows-x86_64 -lib tests/modules/src/vlink/libsrc/beta_static.tiko -o build/.vls/pkg/vendor/beta/lib/beta_windows_x86_64.a
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/modules/src/vlink/app/static.tiko -o build/.vls/static.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.vls/alpha_windows_x86_64.dll
'' RUN: build/.vls/static.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1             alpha header: static
